# Input parameters for ADAF model:
# 1.5d0 - gamma - adiabatic index
# 1.6d2 - m - black hole mass (in 10^6 Solar masses)
# 0.9d0 - beta - ratio of gas to total pressure
# 0.3d0 - alpha viscosity
# 0.1d0 - delta - fraction of viscous energy that directly heats electrons
# 3.1d-4 - mdot_out (Eddington units)
# 1.d4 - R_out (units of R_S)
# 0.3d0 - p_wind - "strength of wind"
# BOUNDARY CONDITIONS ***********
# 0.2 - T_i/T_vir - ion temperature
# 0.19 - T_e/T_vir - electron temperature
# 0.2d0 - v_R/c_s - radial velocity/sound speed
# 2.12 - eigenvalue of the problem ("shooting" parameter)
#
# Auxiliary values:
# 0.36e+9 - T_vir - Virial temperature at the outer boundary
#
# Meaning of columns below:
# 1. radius
# 2. v_R/c_s
# 3. log(T_e)
# 4. log(T_i)
# 5. q_advi/q_vis
# 6. (q_advi+q_adve)/q_vis
# 7. c_s/c
# 8. H
# 9. q_rad (cooling rate/volume)
# 10. tau (optical depth)
# 11. log(l_k) (spec. ang. mom. Kepl.)
# 12. log(l) (spec. ang. mom.)
# 13. magnetic field
# 14. log(rho) [g/cm^3]
# 15. log(ne) [1/cm^3]
#
